<title>FRANCE: France deports 89 illegal immigrants.</title>
<headline>France deports 89 illegal immigrants.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>France on Wednesday deported 89 Moroccans and Malians in a continuing crackdown on illegal immigrants, the Interior Ministry said.</p>
<p>It said 47 Malians and 30 Moroccans were placed on a government-chartered flight to Casablanca and Bamako, the 34th such flight since President Jacques Chirac took power 21 months ago. Another 12 Moroccans were deported on a scheduled flight.</p>
<p>The ministry said 20,679 illegal immigrants had been deported under Chirac.</p>
